//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano
//
// Exercises the seq-first variant with the q-block loop inside the segment
// (--q-in-segment): the same design, herd, cascade and microkernels as the
// default schedule, but the q-block index is an air.sequential loop in the
// segment and herd instead of a launch-grid axis, so the runtime sequence has
// head_groups waves rather than q_blocks * head_groups. GQA shape (12 q / 6 kv
// heads) so the kv-head mapping is covered as well. The output is
// bit-identical to the default schedule's; this test checks it against the
// NumPy reference like the other FlashAttention tests.
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_npu2_peano_seqfirst_q_in_segment
// RUN: cd test_npu2_peano_seqfirst_q_in_segment
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile clean PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile run SCRIPT=attn_npu2_seqfirst.py NUM_HEADS=12 NUM_KV_HEADS=6 EXTRA_PY_FLAGS=--q-in-segment PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR | FileCheck %s
// CHECK: PASS!
